            Buy a 5,000 watt generator if you want real home backup at the lowest weight, price and fuel burn, and you are willing to run the big loads in turns. Make sure it has a 120/240V L14-30R outlet and connect it through a transfer switch. The Westinghouse WGen5300DF is the best all-round choice, the Generac GP5500E is the strongest and the easiest to store, and the DuroMax XP5500EH is the value pick.
          </p>
